      "question": {
        ":question/id": "903e7168-95b7-5bad-a739-c6d09fdecd73",
        ":question/problem": "$$\nf(y,z)=\u27e8\\text{___},\\,y,\\,z\u27e9\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(y,z)$ above parametrizes the parabolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $x=3{y}^{2}.$ What is the first component of $f?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "For any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y,z) & =\u27e8x,y,z\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83{y}^{2},\\,y,\\,z\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the first component of $f$ is $3{y}^{2}.$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
